{
	title: 'Model picker tree like the old Hal',
	spec: "The model picker is the old Hal's tree (tasks/w4/forms.md, Model picker): provider, family or vendor, models; ▶/▼ show closed and open categories, right/left open and close them, Enter on a category picks its default (gpt → the deliberately promoted GPT default (gpt-6.1-sol currently), opus → opus 5.5). A provider's families go most capable first (fable, opus, sonnet, haiku, then by name); in a family, newest version first and same-version variants plain, sol, terra, luna, then by name. A family lists its two newest versions' flagship variants (plain, sol, terra, luna, astra: gpt 6 and 5.6, opus 5.5 and 5); its older versions and other variants (mini, pro, codex, daybreak…) wait in a closed family/older category. A direct provider with families puts non-chat models (image, realtime, audio, tts, transcribe, embedding, moderation, search…) and family-less ones (o3) in a closed provider/other. These buckets come last in their category and have no default, so Enter opens them. A dated snapshot (-20251101) hides behind its undated alias; the current model always shows, its categories open. Rows use the models.dev name as is. Typing matches categories too and selects the matching one first (gp → openai/gpt, opus → anthropic/opus), else the best-scoring model; ties go to an alias's model (claude → Opus 5.5), else to the higher row. Left and right open and close categories even while searching (the search box keeps its text; Ctrl-A/E move in it); typing reopens every matching category, except that older and other stay closed while their parent has matches outside them (gpt keeps gpt/older closed; gpt 5.5 opens it). The typed words show bold and bright in the list (terminal and web) where a word of the row starts, by common/fuzzy.ts, which the find modal will reuse. Modal text fields have Ctrl-A/E, Ctrl-U/K and Alt-Backspace (Ctrl-W stays close-tab). Modals are 80% of the rows, at most 36. On the web, tree indentation is preserved but rows wrap to the available width: complete display names, model IDs and category defaults remain readable on phones without horizontal scrolling or clipping, including with highlighted search matches. The title wraps long current-model IDs too. Touch rows remain at least 44px high. On coarse-pointer devices the picker fills the visual viewport above the keyboard with only a small edge margin, using its live height and offset rather than layout-viewport vh; keyboard resizing or panning leaves no wasted bottom gap and keeps search, close and the scrollable list visible. The phone picker also uses visual-viewport width and horizontal offset, keeping its controls inside the visible rectangle during page zoom. The picker and generic GPT alias share the deliberately promoted default. Listed models need not work on a given account, so a newly listed Sol is visible for explicit selection but never silently becomes the default.",
